 starts with  who  well i mean i think uh  oklahoma's sort of a unique place  they've  at one time in their history literally  have they hired a sitting head coach  that was howard schnellenberger in 1995  it was a disaster he lasted one year  they've always hired an up-and-coming  assistant coach they believe in their  program more than personality  barry switzer bob stoops  chuck fairbanks bud wilkinson i mean all  the big names had never been head  coaches before they got to oklahoma so  uh  that's not necessarily what they'll do  now the transfor portal changes  everything  in the past when you change coaches you  had to worry about your future rosters  and recruiting now you got to worry  about your current roster keeping people  together uh you need sort of a steady  hand that could mean uh that could mean  uh an immediate uh  wisdom is needed guys who can keep the  ship going  in terms of names being thrown around  shane beamer at south carolina he was on  lincoln staff until a year ago  he's he's a guy to look for because very  impressive  the beamer family is as classy  and as well respected as any in america  and that's not just frank shane is the  same way oh you loved him if he was  still on lincoln staff i think he'd  already have been named head coach  so he's one to keep an eye on uh the  sooners we'll talk to brent venables  also 13-year assistant of bob for bob  stoops went to clemson 10 years ago and  has helped dabo swinney build an empire  uh he's only 50. been coaching  uh you know 25 years in college football  but he's only 50 years old he will be a  viable candidate and i think ou will  look at some of the some of the hot  coaches the guy i think to keep an eye  on is matt rule  who did wonderful at baylor he's always  wanted to coach in the nfl he's now been  there two years  i don't know if he likes it i know that  if you go to the nfl and don't have a  quarterback  it's not that great of a job so is matt  ruhl ready to come back to college 